@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki Entitlement Integration
	Testing to assure koroneiki entitlement integration works properly.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I tear down the contact entitlement definitions on koroneiki with the following name values
	| DXP Customer |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| A Liferay DXP Product |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Liferay DXP Product |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Account Role    |
	| NonLiferay Account Role |
 	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORONEKORONE |
	* I tear down the sandbox users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the sandbox users with the following email addresses from the support organization "Koroneiki DXP Customer"
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the sandbox organizations with the following names from customer.liferay.com
	| Koroneiki DXP Customer |

Scenario: Sync user and organization via Koroneiki
	Koroneiki contacts with the proper entitlements synced via Koroneiki should be properly synced to OSB if the OSB site contains the appropriate organization.

	Given I create a sandbox user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a sandbox user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create a koroneiki user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a koroneiki user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Notes                 | Additional account notes             |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Sold By               | Liferay US                           |
	| Status                | Approved                             |
	| Tier                  | Regular                              |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with a koroneiki uuid and the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with a koroneiki uuid and the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the Liferay role for accounts |
	| Name        | Liferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account                               |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the NonLiferay role for accounts |
	| Name        | NonLiferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account                                  |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles	
	| Liferay Account Role |
	And I create a product with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "A Liferay DXP Product" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}   |                |
	| Perpetual               | true               |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1    | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2    | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3    | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                  |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate} |                |
	And I create a contact entitlement definition related to the product purchase of the product "A Liferay DXP Product" and contact role with the name "Liferay Account Role" and type "Account" with the following values
	| Description | DXP Customer Entitlement |
	| Name        | DXP Customer             |
	| Status      | Approved                 |
	And I create a support sandbox organization with the name "Koroneiki DXP Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "DXP Customer"
	Then the organization "Koroneiki DXP Customer" should have the user with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a member

Scenario: Resync user and organization via OSB
	Koroneiki contacts with the proper entitlements resynced via OSB should be properly synced to OSB if the OSB site contains the appropriate organization.

	Given I create a sandbox user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a sandbox user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create a koroneiki user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a koroneiki user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Notes                 | Additional account notes             |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Sold By               | Liferay US                           |
	| Status                | Approved                             |
	| Tier                  | Regular                              |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with a koroneiki uuid and the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with a koroneiki uuid and the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the Liferay role for accounts |
	| Name        | Liferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account                               |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the NonLiferay role for accounts |
	| Name        | NonLiferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account                                  |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles	
	| Liferay Account Role |
	And I create a product with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "A Liferay DXP Product" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}   |                |
	| Perpetual               | true               |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1    | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2    | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3    | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                  |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate} |                |
	And I create a contact entitlement definition related to the product purchase of the product "A Liferay DXP Product" and contact role with the name "Liferay Account Role" and type "Account" with the following values
	| Description | DXP Customer Entitlement |
	| Name        | DXP Customer             |
	| Status      | Approved                 |
	And I create a support sandbox organization with the name "Koroneiki DXP Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "DXP Customer"
	Then the organization "Koroneiki DXP Customer" should have the user with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a member
	When I delete the user with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" from customer.liferay.com
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	And I resync the entitlement "Koroneiki DXP Customer" on OSB
	Then the organization "Koroneiki DXP Customer" should have the user with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a member